  "articleBody": "Even smaller kitchen upgrades can go sideways if you're not careful. To ensure your project goes smoothly and you end up with a kitchen you love, watch out for these common pitfalls:\n\n*   **Choosing style over function first:** It's tempting to pick out pretty finishes, but if your kitchen doesn't function well, those beautiful elements won't matter. Focus on solving your biggest functional problems first.\n*   **Skipping precise measurements:** Eyeballing won't cut it. Accurate measurements are absolutely critical for new appliances, custom cabinetry, or even just fitting a new lighting fixture. Inaccurate measurements lead to costly reorders and delays.\n*   **Underbuying storage solutions:** Most people want more storage in their kitchen. Don't underestimate this! Think about clever organizers, pantry pull-outs, and vertical storage to maximize every inch.\n*   **Neglecting under-cabinet lighting:** This might seem minor, but good task lighting under your cabinets makes a huge difference for food prep and overall ambiance. It's an upgrade that truly enhances usability.\n*   **Not planning enough outlets or counter space:** In today's kitchens, we need more power and more room to work. Think about where you use small appliances and plan for ample outlets and dedicated counter zones.\n*   **Underestimating costs and timelines:** Even for upgrades, unexpected issues can pop up. Always build in a buffer for both budget and schedule. A reputable contractor like HH Remodeling LLC can give you a realistic estimate for your upgrade project.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
